.SH BUGS
One vCPU per machine.
.PP
VMX: a full Linux boot has been shown only on SVM (QEMU's TCG emulates
SVM, not VMX); on VMX the freestanding test passes and Linux boots
partway under Bochs.  A guest's debug registers DR0\-DR3 and DR6 are
kept and read back but not loaded, so its hardware breakpoints do not
fire.  No VPID; the TLB is flushed on every entry and exit.
.PP
Assignment: memory BARs only, MSI-X only, no extended configuration
space, no function reset, and only a function the host has no driver
for.  An assigned function's interrupt raised on another processor is
seen at the vCPU's next exit, at most a clock tick later.
.PP
No XSAVE state beyond x87/SSE is offered to guests.
